<!--/Post: 2330-->
<!--Post: 2462--><!--Time: 1103703391-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2462"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Artimis<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Artimis<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 22, 2004 - 12:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I Think, If I remeber right, the school called her house when she didn&#39;t show up to pick her daughter for lunch and when there was no answer and lunch had come and gone the school called her husband. That&#39;s why he came home. She was very into her kids and very dependable.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2462-->
<!--Post: 2573--><!--Time: 1103818505-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2573"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 8:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I personally don&#39;t believe this is a true BTK case.  I feel that the true killer of Vicky was very clever in that he researched all of the available information regarding BTK, of which there was a mountain of information last January after the 30 year anniversary of the Otero murders.   <BR> <BR>I feel Vicky&#39;s true killer does not fit the profile of BTK and put this &#34;confession&#34; together in order to cast suspicions away from him.  As most people know, Vicky&#39;s husband has long been the prime suspect in her murder.  If he were indeed her killer, he would not fit the profile of BTK, primarily due to his age.   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2573-->
<!--Post: 2592--><!--Time: 1103831556-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2592"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cyndi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cyndi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 23, 2004 - 11:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->So Thinker, are you suggesting that the &#34;real&#34; killer of Mrs. Wegerle stirred up the whole BTK revival by sending a copy of her drivers license to KAKE under the guise of BTK?  Thus the real BTK has jumped on the band wagon &#40;so to speak&#41; by sending/leaving clues of other murders?  If this is the case why would the killer of Mrs. Wegerle dare to risk exposing himself by bringing it all up again &#40;assuming the killer isn&#39;t BTK&#41;?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2592-->
<!--Post: 2594--><!--Time: 1103833615-->
