<!--Post: 3014--><!--Time: 1104371545-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3014"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 5:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe that BTK so enjoys media attention that he could not resist taunting the media once again.  When he saw how this revelation continued to bring him headlines, he couldn&#39;t resist. My reason for feeling Vicky was not a true BTK victim is simple: I feel that the time frame between Vicky and the other victims was too great for him to just have vanished.  That is why I offer the theory that Vicky&#39;s killer was not BTK.  As for Cyndi&#39;s smug statement concerning Vicky&#39;s real killer sending items to the media to stir up BTK, that was already done in January when the Wichita Eagle ran article after article and the local news stations had virtually non-stop coverage of the anniversary of the Otero murders.  The answer to why her real killer would do this is simple.  He is sick and tired of being a suspect.  As I said, we all know that her husband has been the prime suspect since the murder.  This &#34;confession&#34; by BTK to her murder would take all the heat off of him for good.  Sounds like a feasible explanation to me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3014-->
<!--Post: 3015--><!--Time: 1104372414-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3015"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Thinker, just wanted to let you know that people close to Vicki visit upon occasion and they are sensitive to her name being spelled properly. It&#39;s Vicki with an &#34;i.&#34; Lots of people make that mistake and this isn&#39;t meant to be directed at you, but rather a heads-up to everyone.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3015-->
<!--Post: 3063--><!--Time: 1104413152-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3063"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 5:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you, Tom.  I appreciate that.  I can certainly understand the frustration of the situation to the families, without having to face any mispellings towards any of the victims.  My opinions here are geared at forcing people to think outside the boxes we&#39;ve built and I certainly intend no disrespect to the victims or the families.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3063-->
<!--Post: 3088--><!--Time: 1104443024-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3088"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Alobster7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Alobster7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 1:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just curious as to why everyone seemed to suspect Mrs. Wegerle&#39;s husband as her killer.  Were there serious marital problems?  This would be a horrible thing to be accused of for so many years. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3088-->
<!--Post: 3095--><!--Time: 1104448842-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3095"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 3:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The husband was suspected because that is where suspicion often turns when there are no other leads.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3095-->
<!--Post: 3174--><!--Time: 1104547829-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3174"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lanena<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lanena<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 6:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Alobster7:  He was the one who found Vicki, which makes him look a little suspicious.  I also know that he was uncooperative with the police in their investigation.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3174-->
<!--Post: 6506--><!--Time: 1107839134-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6506"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 9:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Because of homicide statistics alone, the husband would be a suspect, regardless, until the police had thoroughly ruled him out. He&#39;d be the first one looked at.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6506-->
<!--Post: 6599--><!--Time: 1107904830-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6599"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 3:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Can anyone tell me Vicki&#39;s maiden name and date of marriage ? <BR> <BR>Thanks.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6599-->
